BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Lecture
DESCRIPTION:In What Sense Are Partitions and Trees "The Same"? -\nPartition
 s of a finite set\, and trees with finitely many leaves\, are two mathemati
 cal structures that we typically come across in very different contexts. In
  this talk\, we will use ideas from category theory and homotopy theory to 
 establish a connection between these two structures. We will investigate pr
 ecisely in which sense they can be considered to be "the same"\, and outlin
 e some interesting consequences of this comparison.
DTEND:20260402T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
DTSTART:20260402T224000Z
GEO:45.480972;-122.630792
LOCATION:Eliot Hall\, 314
