BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Lecture
DESCRIPTION:Power Analysis of Two Sequential Designs: Biased Coin versus Eh
 renfest Urn Models -\nThe power of a statistical test is the probability of
  correctly detecting a treatment effect.  In a randomized trial where two t
 reatments are compared\, the power also depends on the number of assignment
 s of each treatment.  In this presentation\, we will use a simple Student's
  t-test to demonstrate and analyze the power functions of two sequential tr
 eatment allocation designs: the biased coin design and the Ehrenfest urn mo
 del. In particular\, we will discuss the Markovian processes under both des
 igns and provide an eigen-analysis of their transition matrices.
DTEND:20260409T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
DTSTART:20260409T224000Z
GEO:45.480972;-122.630792
LOCATION:Eliot Hall\, 314
SEQUENCE:0
