BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Community
DESCRIPTION:Reed College Choirs\, Division of the Arts\, Music Department\,
  and Comparative Race & Ethnicity Studies presents\n\nHaitham Haidar\, teno
 r\n\nwith pianist Rebecca Stager\n\nfeaturing Reed College Chorus and Colle
 gium Musicum Fri Apr 10\, 2026Doors open at 7:00pmRecital begins at 7:30pmR
 eedwood Friends Church2901 SE Steele St.Free and open to the public Join us
  Friday\, April 10 for a vocal recital and Q&A with Arts Divisional Guest A
 rtist Haitham Haidar\, with pianist Rebecca Stager and featuring Reed Colle
 ge's Chorus and Collegium Musicum. “A gripping communicator and charismatic
  musician” (Gramophone)\, Haitham Haidar is a Lebanese-Palestinian Canadian
  tenor highly sought out for his “arresting warmth and lyricism” (Music Web
  International) and “memorably warm tone” (Gramophone). Haitham’s debut sol
 o album\, Zaytoun\, which explores the intersectionalities of Baroque and A
 rabic music alongside poetry and musical improvisations\, was JUNO® nominat
 ed for Classical Album of the Year: Solo Artist\, picked as BBC Music’s Voc
 al Choice of the Month in October 2025\, and praised as “exquisitely beauti
 ful and inherently melancholic” (Gramophone). Haitham also appears on multi
 ple Grammy® nominated albums\, including as a featured vocalist on Conspira
 re’s House of Belonging.\n\nHaitham has performed as a soloist at the Morge
 nland Music Festival in Osnabrück\, as the Evangelist in Bach’s Christmas O
 ratorio with Seattle Bach Festival\, as Matthew in Considering Matthew Shep
 ard at ACDA Northwestern\, and with groups like Conspirare and Seraphic Fir
 e. He has also been tenor soloist in Handel’s Messiah with Newfoundland Sym
 phony\, Winnipeg Symphony Orchestra\, Arion Baroque Orchestra\, and Spire V
 ocal Ensemble. Recently\, he appeared as the Evangelist in Bach’s St. John 
 Passion with the Choir of A&P in Montreal\, will do so again with Cantata C
 ollective and Nicholas McGegan in June\, and will sing as the Shepherd in E
 arly Music Vancouver’s Orfeo in July.\n\nHaitham is a member of Kaleidoscop
 e Vocal Ensemble\, a group that unites music excellence and diversity while
  offering highly educational and practical experiences to students from mid
 dle school to graduate school. KVE launched the first inaugural Kaleidoscop
 e Vocal Academy in 2025 and the group looks forward to this growing educati
 onal program.\n\nHaitham’s approach to performance has always been humanity
  first. Being an Arab immigrant in North America comes with its unique set 
 of oppressive challenges and it is because of that and what he sees around 
 him in the field\, that he aims to touch people’s hearts with music and com
 passion and make change in the world the best way he knows how. Haitham is 
 a graduate of Yale's Institute of Sacred Music\, McGill's Schulich School o
 f Music\, and the University of British Columbia and currently resides in M
 ontreal\, Quebec.
DTEND:20260411T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
DTSTART:20260411T020000Z
GEO:45.485215;-122.635717
LOCATION:Reedwood Friends Church
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Vocal Recital: Haitham Haidar\, tenor
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52314006434399
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/vocal-recital-haitham-haidar-tenor
END:VEVENT
