BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:The Reed Music Department is pleased to host a lecture-recital 
 presented by local professional vocal ensemble In Mulieribus\, featuring tw
 o of our private voice instructors\, Sarah Beaty and Madeline Ross.\n\nIn M
 ulieribus\, a Portland-based women’s chamber vocal ensemble\, offers a lect
 ure-recital titled “Sappho: Whispers of Desire" that centers on the endurin
 g legacy of Sappho\, the extraordinarily prolific and influential poet of a
 ncient Greece. Though her lyric poetry revolutionized the genre\, Sappho’s 
 voice has been historically marginalized. This project aims to help restore
  a misunderstood and eclipsed figure to her rightful place in cultural hist
 ory through the performance of musical settings of Sappho’s poetry\, spanni
 ng composers from Brahms to contemporary voices.\n\nRenowned classics schol
 ar Dr. Ellen Greene\, author of the first anthology of Sappho scholarship w
 hose research examines diverse critical approaches to her poetry\, will off
 er insights into the curated repertoire and provide contextual understandin
 g of Sappho’s life and work.
DTEND:20260416T201000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
DTSTART:20260416T191000Z
GEO:45.480983;-122.634105
LOCATION:Performing Arts Building\, 320
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sappho: Whispers of Desire Lecture-Recital
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51880642978534
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/sappho-whispers-of-desire-lecture-recital
END:VEVENT
