BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Workshop/Training
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will provide a guided close listening of Alice Co
 ltrane's Universal Consciousness (1971) and Lord of Lords (1972). A central
  theme of the workshop will be how Coltrane stages philosophical questions 
 through her decisions as an artist and spiritual leader. Participants are e
 ncouraged to read pre-circulated excerpts from The Musician as Philosopher:
  New York's Vernacular Avant-Garde (University of Chicago Press\, 2024). Th
 e book's Introduction and the Coltrane chapter will be the focus of discuss
 ion\; for those interested\, Chapters 1 and 2 develop the book's theoretica
 l framework in greater detail.\n\nSponsored by The Evelyn Herold Colloquium
  Series in Humanities and the Film and Media Studies program. Free and open
  to the public.
DTEND:20260417T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
DTSTART:20260417T200000Z
GEO:45.480644;-122.627381
LOCATION:Psych 105
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Evelyn Herold Colloquium Series in Humanities Presents: "The Mu
 sician as Philosopher: Listening to Alice Coltrane"
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52399912461110
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/the-musician-as-philosopher-listening-to-
 alice-coltrane
END:VEVENT
