BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Conference/Symposium
DESCRIPTION:ASN Symposium\, April 18 and 19\, 2026\n\nPlease join the Asian
  Solidarity Network (ASN) on Saturday\, April 18 and Sunday\, April 19 for 
 our second annual Symposium!! The ASN Symposium is a student organized even
 t centering Asian/American diasporic youth. Connect with students\, artists
 \, community organizers\, grassroots groups\, and more\, about politics and
  campaigns waged locally.\n\nProgram website\n\nSchedule linked here (comin
 g soon)\n\n \n\nThis Year's Theme: Envisioning Boundlessness\n\nWhat does i
 t mean to envision boundlessness? \n\nOur intention is to ground ourselves 
 in the moment and conversations happening within the Asian diaspora around 
 socially constructed understandings of borders\, revolution\, legality\, an
 d morality\, all of which are being challenged and deconstructed. Our hope 
 is the symposium becomes a space where participants enter\, committed to fu
 rthering ourselves and extending action outwards. \n\nThus\, our theme is a
  call to action to grow our understanding collectively of what it means to 
 both dismantle and also acknowledge that our work does not end there. We mu
 st be boundless with both our solidarity and our imaginations when we commi
 t to this task.\n\nWe reflect on the limitations of boundaries\, both physi
 cal and not\, and how it affirms ideas of isolation. Across our two day con
 vening of presentations\, discussions\, and workshops we want to deepen our
  understandings and abilities on how to move forward in solidarity–across n
 ational lines\, across generations\, and across identity. \n\nEnvisioning b
 oundlessness is a task we must partake in together\; your interpretations\,
  projects\, and visions will continue to shape our framework so please come
  ready with an open mind and an open heart to this year's \n\nASN Symposium
 \, April 18 and 19\, 2026\n\nClaire\, Dista\, Maya\, Natalie\, and Tika <3
DTEND:20260418T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
DTSTART:20260418T170000Z
GEO:45.480983;-122.634105
LOCATION:Performing Arts Building\, Various
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Asian Solidarity Network Spring Symposium
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52560876108810
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/asian-solidarity-network-spring-symposium
END:VEVENT
