BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Lecture
DESCRIPTION:The Banach-Tarski Paradox -\nThe so-called "Banach-Tarski parad
 ox" is a kind of mathematical magic trick\, the performance of which goes a
 s follows: the mathemagician takes a solid 3 dimensional ball\, decomposes 
 it into finitely many pieces\, and then reassembles these pieces using only
  ordinary Euclidean translations and rotations into two complete copies of 
 the original ball. In clear violation of the magician's code\, I will expla
 in the trick by giving an accessible proof of this remarkable fact\, and di
 scuss the resolution of this apparent "paradox" in 3 dimensional geometry.
DTEND:20260423T234000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
DTSTART:20260423T224000Z
GEO:45.480972;-122.630792
LOCATION:Eliot Hall\, 314
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Math & Statistics Colloquium: Chris Kottke\, Reed College
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52587563686012
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/math-statistics-colloquium-chris-kottke-r
 eed-college
END:VEVENT
