BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Conference/Symposium
DESCRIPTION:AALAC Workshop\n\n \n\nSaturday\, April 25\n \n\n2 PM —3:50 PM 
   Vollum 120\nOpening and Panel One:  “On Books”\n \n\nJulie Cassiday (Will
 iams College) : "'I loved you like a father': Queer Identity and Russophone
  Boys Love"\nKonstantine Klioutchkine  (Pomona College): “How an Exodus is 
 Made: A Reading of Linor Goralik’s Exodus-22”\nEvgenii Bershtein (Reed Coll
 ege): “Guzel Yakhina’s Eisen\, Its Contexts and Audiences”\n\n \n\n4:10 PM–
 5:30 PM   Vollum 120\nModerated Discussion One:  “On Teaching Russian/Russo
 phone Literatures and Cultures Today”\nIntroduced and led by Anne Dwyer (Po
 mona College)\n\n \n\nSunday\, April 26\n \n\n10 PM–11:50 PM   Vollum 120\n
 Panel Two:  “On Exile” \n\nAnton Svynarenko  (Swarthmore College): “'Sittin
 g Correctly Was Hard': Reading Teffi from the 2020s”\nVictoria Thorstensson
  (Carlton College): "Documenting Exodus-22: The Oral History of Russian Pol
 itical Immigrants to Minnesota In the Classroom and in the Community"\nBret
 t Donohoe   (Amherst College): “Reading\, Writing\, and Teaching Russia's Q
 ueer Diaspora”\n\n \n\n12–1:30 PM   Vollum Lounge\nKeynote Event: Polina Ba
 rskova  and Lev Oborin (both UC Berkeley)\n“Breaking the Waves: Generations
  of Russian Cultural Exile” (A Conversation). \n \n\n2:30PM—4:20 PM   Vollu
 m 120\nPanel Three:  “On Russophonia and Translingualism”\n\nNaomi Caffee (
 Reed College): “‘On Common Ground?’ Russophone Entanglements with Queer\, B
 lack\, and Indigenous Imaginaries”  \nIvan Sokolov (Reed College): “New Poe
 ts\, New Exiles: Translingualism and Translation in the Age of Globalizatio
 n”\nRoman Utkin  (Wesleyan University): "Interrogating the Russophone: Note
 s on Linguistic Sovereignty and/in Exile"\n \n\n4:30 PM—5:50 PM Vollum 120\
 nModerated Discussion Two: “On Teaching the Russian Language Today”\nIntrod
 uced and led by Nila Friedberg (Portland State University)\n \n\nThe panels
  and keynote event are free and open to the public. Participation in the mo
 derated discussions is by invitation only.\n\nFor information email Prof. B
 ershtein at bershtee@reed.edu.\nSponsored by the Alliance to Advance Libera
 l Arts College (AALAC) and Reed College.
DTSTAMP:20260423T022028Z
