BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:
DESCRIPTION:Curious about what it’s like to spend a year pursuing an indepe
 ndent project around the world?\n\nJoin Watson Foundation staff and Watson 
 Fellows on Thursday\, April 30 from noon–1 p.m. pacific time for the Spring
  Watson Webinar to explore the incredible opportunity offered by the Thomas
  J. Watson Fellowship!\n\nStaff and fellows will share insights into the pr
 ogram and the application process in this national webinar.\n\nFeatured Wat
 son Fellows:\n\nJulia Thomas\, 2017 Fellow. “Community Voices: Exploring th
 e Intersections of Storytelling\, Citizenship and Journalism”Tommy Shenoi\,
  2024 Fellow. “Cultivating Transformative Resilience with Global Mycology”A
 bout the Fellowship:\n\nThe mission of the Thomas J. Watson Fellowship Prog
 ram is to offer recent college graduates of unusual promise a year of purpo
 seful\, independent exploration and travel outside of the United States. Fe
 llows conceive original projects and embrace the ensuing journey. They deci
 de where to go\, who to meet and when to change course. They receive a stip
 end of $40\,000 to support them in these endeavors. During the year\, fello
 ws enhance their capacity for resourcefulness\, imagination\, openness\, an
 d leadership and foster their humane and effective participation in the wor
 ld community.\n\n🌍 Curious? Inspired? Wondering if this could be your next 
 step?\n\nCurrent First Years\, Sophomores\, Juniors\, and spring/fall Senio
 rs are all welcome to attend\, as well as international students. The 2027 
 application opens on April 30\, 2026\, for students graduating next academi
 c year.\n\nRegister for the Zoom webinar at the link in this event.
DTEND:20260430T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022029Z
DTSTART:20260430T190000Z
LOCATION:
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Watson Fellowship Webinar
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52677141405995
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/watson-fellowship-webinar-7228
END:VEVENT
