BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Student
DESCRIPTION:The spring MRC book club selection is One Day\, Everyone Will H
 ave Always Been Against This by Omar El Akkad. Reed Librarians picked this 
 book by El Akkad\, a local Portland area author\, not just for its critique
  of western imperialism but for the way the author dissects how language an
 d logic are used to sustain said policy. Part self-reflection\, part memoir
 -style writing- this book is a must for anyone interested in learning about
  how lived experiences can be unpacked through writing against the preserva
 tion of status quo. \n\nCome to this MRC Book Club and Zine Club mash up wh
 ere we will participate in zine prompts inspired by El Akkad's writings! \n
 \nSign-ups are at capacity currently. If you signed up\, you will receive a
 n email on when and where to pick up your book. If you haven't had a chance
  to get a book\, you are still welcome to come to this event and discuss ge
 neral themes!
DTEND:20260506T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022029Z
DTSTART:20260506T210000Z
GEO:45.480964;-122.630146
LOCATION:Library\, Zine Library
