BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:Community
DESCRIPTION:Unlike crosses\, statues\, relics or other sacred objects\, ins
 cribed ancestral tablets mapped one'sancestors genealogically and socially\
 , spatially and temporally\, both securing their existence and making them 
 relevant to the present. Tablets are maps\, but are they also “the mapped\,
 ” sacred in their own right? First Saturday PDX invites you and all descend
 ants and ancestors to this talk with Dr K.E. Brashier who shares his new re
 search about the prescriptions and practices that inform this iconic tradit
 ion\, amply illustrating his talk with as-yet-unpublished images of numerou
 s ancestral tablets and paintings from the 19th and 20th centuries in China
  and its neighbors.
DTEND:20260516T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T022029Z
DTSTART:20260516T163000Z
GEO:45.480644;-122.627381
LOCATION:Psychology\, 105
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mapping Memory via Ancestral Tablets 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52490916609502
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/mapping-memory-via-ancestral-tablets
END:VEVENT
